      "writtenOn": "2022-09-30T14:06:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A-ha!  I bet it\u0027s because the default std::string hash looks at the full string content (hashes size() chars), and doesn\u0027t stop at the first null -- so it includes the \\0 padding at the end from resize().  Initializing a copy from c_str() trims all the padding.  So if you print it out they will look the same, but they are really different as hash keys.\n\nIt might be cleaner to use std::array\u003cchar, kBufferLen\u003e for ImGui buffers, and just create std::strings on the fly (looks like we have to make copies anyway).  That way we don\u0027t have to muck with resize and worry about hashing issues, and can prolly also skip shrink_to_fits.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 367,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 368,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "ee20ffaca18b82a7e997b0525300a9d405dce9f7",
