      "writtenOn": "2022-09-30T14:06:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The problem with storing an sk_sp here is it keeps the slide reference count alive.  So when Viewer unrefs a SkottieSlide, its ref count doesn\u0027t go to zero and it effectively leaks.\n\nSince SkottieSlide owns the wrapper, and is guaranteed to outlive it, it should be fine to store a raw pointer instead (to avoid the refence leak).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 399,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 399,
        "endChar": 23
